{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You have a chat or generation UI and you want users to talk instead of type. By\nthe end of this guide you'll capture microphone audio in the browser with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useAudioRecorder"},{"type":"text","value":", read the latest recording reactively, and send it straight\ninto a chat message or a transcription request, with no transcoding and no\nextra dependencies."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useAudioRecorder"},{"type":"text","value":" wraps the browser's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getUserMedia"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MediaRecorder"},{"type":"text","value":" and\nreturns the recorder's native output ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"audio/webm"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"audio/mp4"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"record-audio","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Record audio"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Start with a button; end with a working recorder that toggles capture and hands\nyou the result."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useAudioRecorder } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nfunction RecordButton() {\n  const { isRecording, isSupported, start, stop } = useAudioRecorder({\n    onError: (error) => console.error(error),\n  })\n\n  if (!isSupported) return <p>Recording is not supported in this browser.</p>\n\n  return (\n    <button onClick={() => (isRecording ? void stop() : void start())}>\n      {isRecording ? 'Stop' : 'Record'}\n    </button>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"group=audio-recording"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stop()"},{"type":"text","value":" resolves to an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AudioRecording"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Field"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"part"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AudioPart"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ready-to-use content part: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ type: 'audio', source: { type: 'data', value, mimeType } }"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"base64"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Raw base64 of the recorded bytes"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"blob"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Blob"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The raw recorded blob"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mimeType"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Native recorder type, e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"audio/webm;codecs=opus"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"durationMs"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recording length in milliseconds"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"handling-errors","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Handling errors"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Failures reach you through "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"two"}]},{"type":"text","value":" channels. Pick one, and do not handle both:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onError(error)"},{"type":"text","value":" fires for permission denial and recorder errors."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"start()"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stop()"},{"type":"text","value":" also "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"reject"}]},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"start()"},{"type":"text","value":" rejects on permission\ndenial; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stop()"},{"type":"text","value":" rejects on a recorder error or with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Recording cancelled"},{"type":"text","value":" if\nthe recording is cancelled while a stop is in flight (for example when the\ncomponent unmounts mid-recording)."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"So if you "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"await start()"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"await stop()"},{"type":"text","value":", wrap them in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"try"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"catch"},{"type":"text","value":" rather\nthan discarding the promise with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"},{"type":"text","value":". The recorder's native "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mimeType"},{"type":"text","value":" may\ndiffer from a requested "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mimeType"},{"type":"text","value":" (browsers ignore unsupported types), so read\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recording.mimeType"},{"type":"text","value":" if a downstream step requires a specific format."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"read-the-latest-recording-reactively","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read the latest recording reactively"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The same value is also exposed as the reactive "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recording"},{"type":"text","value":" field, so you can\nrender a preview without capturing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stop()"},{"type":"text","value":"'s return value yourself. It's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":"\nuntil the first "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stop()"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function Preview() {\n  const { recording, isRecording, start, stop } = useAudioRecorder()\n  // recording is AudioRecording | null\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"group=audio-recording"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Across frameworks "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recording"},{"type":"text","value":" follows the same shape as the other reactive\nfields: an accessor in Solid ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recording()"},{"type":"text","value":"), a readonly ref in Vue\n("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recording.value"},{"type":"text","value":"), a getter in Svelte ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recorder.recording"},{"type":"text","value":"), and a\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Signal"},{"type":"text","value":" in Angular ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recording()"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"transform-the-recording","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Transform the recording"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onComplete"},{"type":"text","value":" to turn the raw recording into whatever your app needs: a URL\nafter upload, an encoded blob, or a custom object. Both "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stop()"},{"type":"text","value":" and the\nreactive "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recording"},{"type":"text","value":" field then resolve to your transformed value, and the\ntransform can be "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"async"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function Uploader() {\n  const { recording, stop } = useAudioRecorder({\n    onComplete: async (rec) => {\n      const res = await fetch('/api/upload', { method: 'POST', body: rec.blob })\n      const { url } = await res.json()\n      return url // `recording` and `stop()` now resolve to string\n    },\n  })\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"group=audio-recording"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return nothing ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":") to keep the raw "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AudioRecording"},{"type":"text","value":"; any returned\nvalue (including "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":") is used as-is and re-types "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stop()"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recording"},{"type":"text","value":".\nThis is similar to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onResult"},{"type":"text","value":" transform on the\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./generation-hooks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"generation hooks"}]},{"type":"text","value":", but is async-capable. (Unlike\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onResult"},{"type":"text","value":", where "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" means \"keep the previous value,\" only "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":" keeps\nthe raw recording here.)"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"send-a-recording-in-chat","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Send a recording in chat"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The recording's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"part"},{"type":"text","value":" is already a chat content part, so it drops straight into\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sendMessage"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  useAudioRecorder,\n  useChat,\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nfunction VoiceComposer() {\n  const { isRecording, start, stop } = useAudioRecorder()\n  const { sendMessage } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n  })\n\n  const toggle = async () => {\n    try {\n      if (!isRecording) {\n        await start()\n        return\n      }\n      const rec = await stop()\n      await sendMessage({ content: [rec.part] })\n    } catch (error) {\n      // start()/stop() reject on permission denial, recorder error, or cancel.\n      console.error(error)\n    }\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <button onClick={() => void toggle()}>\n      {isRecording ? 'Send' : 'Record'}\n    </button>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"transcribe-a-recording","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Transcribe a recording"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wrap the recording as a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data:"},{"type":"text","value":" URL so the provider receives the recorder's\nnative content type. Passing raw "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"base64"},{"type":"text","value":" makes the transcription adapter\nassume "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"audio/mpeg"},{"type":"text","value":" and mislabel the webm/mp4 bytes. See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./transcription","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Transcription"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the matching server route."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  useAudioRecorder,\n  useTranscription,\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nfunction Transcriber() {\n  const { isRecording, start, stop } = useAudioRecorder()\n  const { generate, result } = useTranscription({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/transcribe'),\n  })\n\n  const toggle = async () => {\n    try {\n      if (!isRecording) {\n        await start()\n        return\n      }\n      const rec = await stop()\n      // Wrap as a data URL so the provider gets the recorder's real content\n      // type. Passing raw base64 makes the transcription adapter assume\n      // `audio/mpeg`, which mislabels the native webm/mp4 bytes. Strip the\n      // `;codecs=...` parameter for a clean type.\n      const mimeType = rec.mimeType.split(';')[0]\n      await generate({ audio: `data:${mimeType};base64,${rec.base64}` })\n    } catch (error) {\n      console.error(error)\n    }\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button onClick={() => void toggle()}>\n        {isRecording ? 'Stop' : 'Record'}\n      </button>\n      {result ? <p>{result.text}</p> : null}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"other-frameworks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Other frameworks"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The same recorder ships for every framework with idiomatic reactivity. Svelte\nuses the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createAudioRecorder"},{"type":"text","value":" factory; because Svelte 5 runes can't register\nautomatic teardown, call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cancel()"},{"type":"text","value":" from your component cleanup if a recording\nmay still be active:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import {\n    createAudioRecorder,\n    createChat,\n    fetchServerSentEvents,\n  } from '@tanstack/ai-svelte'\n\n  const recorder = createAudioRecorder()\n  const chat = createChat({ connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat') })\n\n  async function toggle() {\n    if (!recorder.isRecording) {\n      await recorder.start()\n      return\n    }\n    const rec = await recorder.stop()\n    await chat.sendMessage({ content: [rec.part] })\n  }\n</script>\n\n<button onclick={toggle}>{recorder.isRecording ? 'Send' : 'Record'}</button>","lang":"svelte"},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Framework"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Function"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reactive fields"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-react"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useAudioRecorder"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isRecording"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recording"},{"type":"text","value":" (values)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Solid"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-solid"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useAudioRecorder"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isRecording()"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recording()"},{"type":"text","value":" (accessors)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vue"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-vue"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useAudioRecorder"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isRecording.value"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recording.value"},{"type":"text","value":" (readonly refs)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Svelte"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-svelte"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createAudioRecorder"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recorder.isRecording"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recorder.recording"},{"type":"text","value":" (getters)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Angular"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-angular"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectAudioRecorder"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isRecording()"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recording()"},{"type":"text","value":" (signals; call in an injection context)"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"hook-api","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hook API"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useAudioRecorder(options?)"},{"type":"text","value":" and its "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createAudioRecorder"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectAudioRecorder"},{"type":"text","value":"\nequivalents accept:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onComplete"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(recording: AudioRecording) => T | Promise<T>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional transform. Its (awaited) return re-types "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stop()"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recording"},{"type":"text","value":". Return nothing to keep the raw recording"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onError"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(error: Error) => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Called on permission denial or recorder error"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"audio"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MediaTrackConstraints | boolean"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Passed to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getUserMedia({ audio })"},{"type":"text","value":". Defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mimeType"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Preferred recorder mime type; falls back to the browser default if unsupported"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"And return:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Property"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recording"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"T | null"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Latest recording (transformed if "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onComplete"},{"type":"text","value":" provided), reactive"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isRecording"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Whether capture is currently active"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isSupported"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Whether the browser supports recording"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"start"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"() => Promise<void>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Acquire the mic and begin recording"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stop"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"() => Promise<T>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stop, and resolve with the recording (transformed if applicable)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cancel"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"() => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Discard the in-progress recording and release the mic"}]}]]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reactive shapes ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recording"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isRecording"},{"type":"text","value":") vary per framework. See the\ntable in "},{"type":"link","href":"#other-frameworks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Other frameworks"}]},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"T"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AudioRecording"},{"type":"text","value":"\nunless an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onComplete"},{"type":"text","value":" transform changes it."}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"record-audio","text":"Record audio","level":2},{"id":"handling-errors","text":"Handling errors","level":2},{"id":"read-the-latest-recording-reactively","text":"Read the latest recording reactively","level":2},{"id":"transform-the-recording","text":"Transform the recording","level":2},{"id":"send-a-recording-in-chat","text":"Send a recording in chat","level":2},{"id":"transcribe-a-recording","text":"Transcribe a recording","level":2},{"id":"other-frameworks","text":"Other frameworks","level":2},{"id":"hook-api","text":"Hook API","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYou have a chat or generation UI and you want users to talk instead of type. By\nthe end of this guide you'll capture microphone audio in the browser with\n`useAudioRecorder`, read the latest recording reactively, and send it straight\ninto a chat message or a transcription request, with no transcoding and no\nextra dependencies.\n\n`useAudioRecorder` wraps the browser's `getUserMedia` / `MediaRecorder` and\nreturns the recorder's native output (`audio/webm` or `audio/mp4`).\n\n## Record audio\n\nStart with a button; end with a working recorder that toggles capture and hands\nyou the result.\n\n```tsx group=audio-recording\nimport { useAudioRecorder } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nfunction RecordButton() {\n  const { isRecording, isSupported, start, stop } = useAudioRecorder({\n    onError: (error) => console.error(error),\n  })\n\n  if (!isSupported) return <p>Recording is not supported in this browser.</p>\n\n  return (\n    <button onClick={() => (isRecording ? void stop() : void start())}>\n      {isRecording ? 'Stop' : 'Record'}\n    </button>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n`stop()` resolves to an `AudioRecording`:\n\n| Field        | Type        | Description                                                                  |\n| ------------ | ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `part`       | `AudioPart` | Ready-to-use content part: `{ type: 'audio', source: { type: 'data', value, mimeType } }` |\n| `base64`     | `string`    | Raw base64 of the recorded bytes                                             |\n| `blob`       | `Blob`      | The raw recorded blob                                                        |\n| `mimeType`   | `string`    | Native recorder type, e.g. `audio/webm;codecs=opus`                          |\n| `durationMs` | `number`    | Recording length in milliseconds                                             |\n\n## Handling errors\n\nFailures reach you through **two** channels. Pick one, and do not handle both:\n\n- `onError(error)` fires for permission denial and recorder errors.\n- `start()` and `stop()` also **reject**. `start()` rejects on permission\n  denial; `stop()` rejects on a recorder error or with `Recording cancelled` if\n  the recording is cancelled while a stop is in flight (for example when the\n  component unmounts mid-recording).\n\nSo if you `await start()` / `await stop()`, wrap them in `try`/`catch` rather\nthan discarding the promise with `void`. The recorder's native `mimeType` may\ndiffer from a requested `mimeType` (browsers ignore unsupported types), so read\n`recording.mimeType` if a downstream step requires a specific format.\n\n## Read the latest recording reactively\n\nThe same value is also exposed as the reactive `recording` field, so you can\nrender a preview without capturing `stop()`'s return value yourself. It's `null`\nuntil the first `stop()`:\n\n```tsx group=audio-recording\nfunction Preview() {\n  const { recording, isRecording, start, stop } = useAudioRecorder()\n  // recording is AudioRecording | null\n}\n```\n\n> Across frameworks `recording` follows the same shape as the other reactive\n> fields: an accessor in Solid (`recording()`), a readonly ref in Vue\n> (`recording.value`), a getter in Svelte (`recorder.recording`), and a\n> `Signal` in Angular (`recording()`).\n\n## Transform the recording\n\nPass `onComplete` to turn the raw recording into whatever your app needs: a URL\nafter upload, an encoded blob, or a custom object. Both `stop()` and the\nreactive `recording` field then resolve to your transformed value, and the\ntransform can be `async`:\n\n```tsx group=audio-recording\nfunction Uploader() {\n  const { recording, stop } = useAudioRecorder({\n    onComplete: async (rec) => {\n      const res = await fetch('/api/upload', { method: 'POST', body: rec.blob })\n      const { url } = await res.json()\n      return url // `recording` and `stop()` now resolve to string\n    },\n  })\n}\n```\n\nReturn nothing (`undefined`) to keep the raw `AudioRecording`; any returned\nvalue (including `null`) is used as-is and re-types `stop()` and `recording`.\nThis is similar to the `onResult` transform on the\n[generation hooks](./generation-hooks), but is async-capable. (Unlike\n`onResult`, where `null` means \"keep the previous value,\" only `undefined` keeps\nthe raw recording here.)\n\n## Send a recording in chat\n\nThe recording's `part` is already a chat content part, so it drops straight into\n`sendMessage`:\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  useAudioRecorder,\n  useChat,\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nfunction VoiceComposer() {\n  const { isRecording, start, stop } = useAudioRecorder()\n  const { sendMessage } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n  })\n\n  const toggle = async () => {\n    try {\n      if (!isRecording) {\n        await start()\n        return\n      }\n      const rec = await stop()\n      await sendMessage({ content: [rec.part] })\n    } catch (error) {\n      // start()/stop() reject on permission denial, recorder error, or cancel.\n      console.error(error)\n    }\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <button onClick={() => void toggle()}>\n      {isRecording ? 'Send' : 'Record'}\n    </button>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Transcribe a recording\n\nWrap the recording as a `data:` URL so the provider receives the recorder's\nnative content type. Passing raw `base64` makes the transcription adapter\nassume `audio/mpeg` and mislabel the webm/mp4 bytes. See\n[Transcription](./transcription) for the matching server route.\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  useAudioRecorder,\n  useTranscription,\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nfunction Transcriber() {\n  const { isRecording, start, stop } = useAudioRecorder()\n  const { generate, result } = useTranscription({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/transcribe'),\n  })\n\n  const toggle = async () => {\n    try {\n      if (!isRecording) {\n        await start()\n        return\n      }\n      const rec = await stop()\n      // Wrap as a data URL so the provider gets the recorder's real content\n      // type. Passing raw base64 makes the transcription adapter assume\n      // `audio/mpeg`, which mislabels the native webm/mp4 bytes. Strip the\n      // `;codecs=...` parameter for a clean type.\n      const mimeType = rec.mimeType.split(';')[0]\n      await generate({ audio: `data:${mimeType};base64,${rec.base64}` })\n    } catch (error) {\n      console.error(error)\n    }\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button onClick={() => void toggle()}>\n        {isRecording ? 'Stop' : 'Record'}\n      </button>\n      {result ? <p>{result.text}</p> : null}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Other frameworks\n\nThe same recorder ships for every framework with idiomatic reactivity. Svelte\nuses the `createAudioRecorder` factory; because Svelte 5 runes can't register\nautomatic teardown, call `cancel()` from your component cleanup if a recording\nmay still be active:\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import {\n    createAudioRecorder,\n    createChat,\n    fetchServerSentEvents,\n  } from '@tanstack/ai-svelte'\n\n  const recorder = createAudioRecorder()\n  const chat = createChat({ connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat') })\n\n  async function toggle() {\n    if (!recorder.isRecording) {\n      await recorder.start()\n      return\n    }\n    const rec = await recorder.stop()\n    await chat.sendMessage({ content: [rec.part] })\n  }\n</script>\n\n<button onclick={toggle}>{recorder.isRecording ? 'Send' : 'Record'}</button>\n```\n\n| Framework | Import                  | Function             | Reactive fields                                      |\n| --------- | ----------------------- | -------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| React     | `@tanstack/ai-react`    | `useAudioRecorder`   | `isRecording`, `recording` (values)                  |\n| Solid     | `@tanstack/ai-solid`    | `useAudioRecorder`   | `isRecording()`, `recording()` (accessors)           |\n| Vue       | `@tanstack/ai-vue`      | `useAudioRecorder`   | `isRecording.value`, `recording.value` (readonly refs) |\n| Svelte    | `@tanstack/ai-svelte`   | `createAudioRecorder`| `recorder.isRecording`, `recorder.recording` (getters) |\n| Angular   | `@tanstack/ai-angular`  | `injectAudioRecorder`| `isRecording()`, `recording()` (signals; call in an injection context) |\n\n## Hook API\n\n`useAudioRecorder(options?)` and its `createAudioRecorder` / `injectAudioRecorder`\nequivalents accept:\n\n| Option       | Type                                                | Description                                                                                          |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onComplete` | `(recording: AudioRecording) => T \\| Promise<T>`    | Optional transform. Its (awaited) return re-types `stop()` and `recording`. Return nothing to keep the raw recording |\n| `onError`    | `(error: Error) => void`                            | Called on permission denial or recorder error                                                       |\n| `audio`      | `MediaTrackConstraints \\| boolean`                  | Passed to `getUserMedia({ audio })`. Defaults to `true`                                             |\n| `mimeType`   | `string`                                            | Preferred recorder mime type; falls back to the browser default if unsupported                      |\n\nAnd return:\n\n| Property      | Type                  | Description                                                          |\n| ------------- | --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `recording`   | `T \\| null`           | Latest recording (transformed if `onComplete` provided), reactive   |\n| `isRecording` | `boolean`             | Whether capture is currently active                                 |\n| `isSupported` | `boolean`             | Whether the browser supports recording                              |\n| `start`       | `() => Promise<void>` | Acquire the mic and begin recording                                 |\n| `stop`        | `() => Promise<T>`    | Stop, and resolve with the recording (transformed if applicable)    |\n| `cancel`      | `() => void`          | Discard the in-progress recording and release the mic               |\n\n> Reactive shapes (`recording`, `isRecording`) vary per framework. See the\n> table in [Other frameworks](#other-frameworks). `T` is `AudioRecording`\n> unless an `onComplete` transform changes it.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Audio Recording\nid: audio-recording\ndescription: \"Record microphone audio in the browser with useAudioRecorder and send it to a chat or transcription as a ready-to-use content part, with an optional transform.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - audio recording\n  - useAudioRecorder\n  - createAudioRecorder\n  - injectAudioRecorder\n  - voice input\n  - MediaRecorder\n---\n\nYou have a chat or generation UI and you want users to talk instead of type. By\nthe end of this guide you'll capture microphone audio in the browser with\n`useAudioRecorder`, read the latest recording reactively, and send it straight\ninto a chat message or a transcription request, with no transcoding and no\nextra dependencies.\n\n`useAudioRecorder` wraps the browser's `getUserMedia` / `MediaRecorder` and\nreturns the recorder's native output (`audio/webm` or `audio/mp4`).\n\n## Record audio\n\nStart with a button; end with a working recorder that toggles capture and hands\nyou the result.\n\n```tsx group=audio-recording\nimport { useAudioRecorder } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nfunction RecordButton() {\n  const { isRecording, isSupported, start, stop } = useAudioRecorder({\n    onError: (error) => console.error(error),\n  })\n\n  if (!isSupported) return <p>Recording is not supported in this browser.</p>\n\n  return (\n    <button onClick={() => (isRecording ? void stop() : void start())}>\n      {isRecording ? 'Stop' : 'Record'}\n    </button>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n`stop()` resolves to an `AudioRecording`:\n\n| Field        | Type        | Description                                                                  |\n| ------------ | ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `part`       | `AudioPart` | Ready-to-use content part: `{ type: 'audio', source: { type: 'data', value, mimeType } }` |\n| `base64`     | `string`    | Raw base64 of the recorded bytes                                             |\n| `blob`       | `Blob`      | The raw recorded blob                                                        |\n| `mimeType`   | `string`    | Native recorder type, e.g. `audio/webm;codecs=opus`                          |\n| `durationMs` | `number`    | Recording length in milliseconds                                             |\n\n## Handling errors\n\nFailures reach you through **two** channels. Pick one, and do not handle both:\n\n- `onError(error)` fires for permission denial and recorder errors.\n- `start()` and `stop()` also **reject**. `start()` rejects on permission\n  denial; `stop()` rejects on a recorder error or with `Recording cancelled` if\n  the recording is cancelled while a stop is in flight (for example when the\n  component unmounts mid-recording).\n\nSo if you `await start()` / `await stop()`, wrap them in `try`/`catch` rather\nthan discarding the promise with `void`. The recorder's native `mimeType` may\ndiffer from a requested `mimeType` (browsers ignore unsupported types), so read\n`recording.mimeType` if a downstream step requires a specific format.\n\n## Read the latest recording reactively\n\nThe same value is also exposed as the reactive `recording` field, so you can\nrender a preview without capturing `stop()`'s return value yourself. It's `null`\nuntil the first `stop()`:\n\n```tsx group=audio-recording\nfunction Preview() {\n  const { recording, isRecording, start, stop } = useAudioRecorder()\n  // recording is AudioRecording | null\n}\n```\n\n> Across frameworks `recording` follows the same shape as the other reactive\n> fields: an accessor in Solid (`recording()`), a readonly ref in Vue\n> (`recording.value`), a getter in Svelte (`recorder.recording`), and a\n> `Signal` in Angular (`recording()`).\n\n## Transform the recording\n\nPass `onComplete` to turn the raw recording into whatever your app needs: a URL\nafter upload, an encoded blob, or a custom object. Both `stop()` and the\nreactive `recording` field then resolve to your transformed value, and the\ntransform can be `async`:\n\n```tsx group=audio-recording\nfunction Uploader() {\n  const { recording, stop } = useAudioRecorder({\n    onComplete: async (rec) => {\n      const res = await fetch('/api/upload', { method: 'POST', body: rec.blob })\n      const { url } = await res.json()\n      return url // `recording` and `stop()` now resolve to string\n    },\n  })\n}\n```\n\nReturn nothing (`undefined`) to keep the raw `AudioRecording`; any returned\nvalue (including `null`) is used as-is and re-types `stop()` and `recording`.\nThis is similar to the `onResult` transform on the\n[generation hooks](./generation-hooks), but is async-capable. (Unlike\n`onResult`, where `null` means \"keep the previous value,\" only `undefined` keeps\nthe raw recording here.)\n\n## Send a recording in chat\n\nThe recording's `part` is already a chat content part, so it drops straight into\n`sendMessage`:\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  useAudioRecorder,\n  useChat,\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nfunction VoiceComposer() {\n  const { isRecording, start, stop } = useAudioRecorder()\n  const { sendMessage } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n  })\n\n  const toggle = async () => {\n    try {\n      if (!isRecording) {\n        await start()\n        return\n      }\n      const rec = await stop()\n      await sendMessage({ content: [rec.part] })\n    } catch (error) {\n      // start()/stop() reject on permission denial, recorder error, or cancel.\n      console.error(error)\n    }\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <button onClick={() => void toggle()}>\n      {isRecording ? 'Send' : 'Record'}\n    </button>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Transcribe a recording\n\nWrap the recording as a `data:` URL so the provider receives the recorder's\nnative content type. Passing raw `base64` makes the transcription adapter\nassume `audio/mpeg` and mislabel the webm/mp4 bytes. See\n[Transcription](./transcription) for the matching server route.\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  useAudioRecorder,\n  useTranscription,\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nfunction Transcriber() {\n  const { isRecording, start, stop } = useAudioRecorder()\n  const { generate, result } = useTranscription({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/transcribe'),\n  })\n\n  const toggle = async () => {\n    try {\n      if (!isRecording) {\n        await start()\n        return\n      }\n      const rec = await stop()\n      // Wrap as a data URL so the provider gets the recorder's real content\n      // type. Passing raw base64 makes the transcription adapter assume\n      // `audio/mpeg`, which mislabels the native webm/mp4 bytes. Strip the\n      // `;codecs=...` parameter for a clean type.\n      const mimeType = rec.mimeType.split(';')[0]\n      await generate({ audio: `data:${mimeType};base64,${rec.base64}` })\n    } catch (error) {\n      console.error(error)\n    }\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button onClick={() => void toggle()}>\n        {isRecording ? 'Stop' : 'Record'}\n      </button>\n      {result ? <p>{result.text}</p> : null}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Other frameworks\n\nThe same recorder ships for every framework with idiomatic reactivity. Svelte\nuses the `createAudioRecorder` factory; because Svelte 5 runes can't register\nautomatic teardown, call `cancel()` from your component cleanup if a recording\nmay still be active:\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import {\n    createAudioRecorder,\n    createChat,\n    fetchServerSentEvents,\n  } from '@tanstack/ai-svelte'\n\n  const recorder = createAudioRecorder()\n  const chat = createChat({ connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat') })\n\n  async function toggle() {\n    if (!recorder.isRecording) {\n      await recorder.start()\n      return\n    }\n    const rec = await recorder.stop()\n    await chat.sendMessage({ content: [rec.part] })\n  }\n</script>\n\n<button onclick={toggle}>{recorder.isRecording ? 'Send' : 'Record'}</button>\n```\n\n| Framework | Import                  | Function             | Reactive fields                                      |\n| --------- | ----------------------- | -------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| React     | `@tanstack/ai-react`    | `useAudioRecorder`   | `isRecording`, `recording` (values)                  |\n| Solid     | `@tanstack/ai-solid`    | `useAudioRecorder`   | `isRecording()`, `recording()` (accessors)           |\n| Vue       | `@tanstack/ai-vue`      | `useAudioRecorder`   | `isRecording.value`, `recording.value` (readonly refs) |\n| Svelte    | `@tanstack/ai-svelte`   | `createAudioRecorder`| `recorder.isRecording`, `recorder.recording` (getters) |\n| Angular   | `@tanstack/ai-angular`  | `injectAudioRecorder`| `isRecording()`, `recording()` (signals; call in an injection context) |\n\n## Hook API\n\n`useAudioRecorder(options?)` and its `createAudioRecorder` / `injectAudioRecorder`\nequivalents accept:\n\n| Option       | Type                                                | Description                                                                                          |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onComplete` | `(recording: AudioRecording) => T \\| Promise<T>`    | Optional transform. Its (awaited) return re-types `stop()` and `recording`. Return nothing to keep the raw recording |\n| `onError`    | `(error: Error) => void`                            | Called on permission denial or recorder error                                                       |\n| `audio`      | `MediaTrackConstraints \\| boolean`                  | Passed to `getUserMedia({ audio })`. Defaults to `true`                                             |\n| `mimeType`   | `string`                                            | Preferred recorder mime type; falls back to the browser default if unsupported                      |\n\nAnd return:\n\n| Property      | Type                  | Description                                                          |\n| ------------- | --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `recording`   | `T \\| null`           | Latest recording (transformed if `onComplete` provided), reactive   |\n| `isRecording` | `boolean`             | Whether capture is currently active                                 |\n| `isSupported` | `boolean`             | Whether the browser supports recording                              |\n| `start`       | `() => Promise<void>` | Acquire the mic and begin recording                                 |\n| `stop`        | `() => Promise<T>`    | Stop, and resolve with the recording (transformed if applicable)    |\n| `cancel`      | `() => void`          | Discard the in-progress recording and release the mic               |\n\n> Reactive shapes (`recording`, `isRecording`) vary per framework. See the\n> table in [Other frameworks](#other-frameworks). `T` is `AudioRecording`\n> unless an `onComplete` transform changes it.\n"}
